NUM-34: give [GWF] expressions the K of the aquifer being computed

The variable K of a custom groundwater flow expression returns the file-scope
HydCon, which getUpperPerc() sets only when the upper zone is above field
capacity. For a drier aquifer K is whatever an earlier subcatchment (or an
earlier ODE stage) left there, or 0. Compute HydCon = Ks exp((theta - phi)
HCO), the unsaturated conductivity at the current moisture content, in
getFluxes() before the expressions are evaluated, for every aquifer. The
percolation rate is unchanged; K is unchanged wherever it was set before.

Apply from the root of a Stormwater-Management-Model checkout at cb3e192b:
    git apply NUM-34_swmm530.patch

diff --git a/src/legacy/engine/gwater.c b/src/legacy/engine/gwater.c
index d511143..ca32aaf 100644
--- a/src/legacy/engine/gwater.c
+++ b/src/legacy/engine/gwater.c
@@ -660,6 +660,10 @@ void  getFluxes(double theta, double lowerDepth)
     // --- find evaporation rate from both zones
     getEvapRates(theta, upperDepth);
 
+    // --- unsaturated hyd. conductivity at current moisture content
+    //     (variable K of custom GW flow expressions)
+    HydCon = A.conductivity * exp((theta - A.porosity) * A.conductSlope);
+
     // --- find percolation rate from upper to lower zone
     UpperPerc = getUpperPerc(theta, upperDepth);
     UpperPerc = MIN(UpperPerc, MaxUpperPerc);
@@ -800,7 +804,6 @@ double getUpperPerc(double theta, double upperDepth)
     dhdz = 1.0 + A.tensionSlope * 2.0 * delta / upperDepth;
 
     // --- compute upper zone percolation rate
-    HydCon = hydcon;
     return hydcon * dhdz;
 }
 
